{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>In the morning.</b> Its meaning is always, according to both interpretations. The tav of זרע is [vowelized with] tenuach [lenition] in the feminine because of the yod. The sense is: do not let your hands rest from sowing, for we find the word נוח governing two [different] verbs."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:07.908949027Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}